# The port's half of the pi+ like-for-like; its partner is pion_emonly.mac. See muon_port.mac
# for why the two files differ only by the inactivations.
#
# MEASURED, 20,000 events:
#
#   pi+   port 25.1815 +/- 0.133 nGy   Geant4 25.2319 +/- 0.134   -0.20%, 0.27 sigma
#
# The cleanest of the four: a species whose transport this package added, agreeing with Geant4
# to two parts in a thousand on a dose, with no free parameter between them.
#
# RE-MEASURED AT 500,000 events, when the negative pion was added beside it:
#
#   pi+   port 632.349 +/- 0.668 nGy   Geant4 633.446 +/- 0.668   -0.17%, 1.16 sigma
#
# Same answer at twenty-five times the statistics, and it is now one row of six: every positive
# hadron measured agrees inside 0.35% and every negative one is 3.8% to 9.5% high. The negative
# half is pion_minus_port.mac and the reason is in docs/RISK.md, not in the pion.
#
# RE-RUN AFTER THE V46 FIX, same 500,000 events: 632.349 +/- 0.668 nGy, BIT-IDENTICAL. That is
# the point of re-running a positive. The fix changes the interpolation of the dE/dx and range
# tables for the SECOND-registered member of each charge pair, and pi+ is the first; if this
# number had moved by one digit the predicate would be selecting the wrong species. The pi-
# beside it went from 630.922 to 600.871 against Geant4's 600.831.
#
# The event count in this file was 20,000 while its header quoted 500,000-event numbers, which
# the macro as written could not produce - B1 prints a CUMULATIVE dose, so the two counts give
# 25.2 nGy and 632 nGy for the same physics. It is 500,000 now, which is also what the 0.2%
# effect left after the fix needs.

/run/initialize
/control/verbose 0
/run/verbose 0

/gun/particle pi+
/gun/energy 200 MeV

/run/printProgress 100000
/run/beamOn 500000
